WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.241
- I, for the billionth time
on this show,

00:00:03.241 --> 00:00:04.879
am a counter-puncher.

00:00:04.879 --> 00:00:07.997
I react to the opportunities in 
front of me at that moment.

00:00:07.997 --> 00:00:09.828
I'm not predicting here.

00:00:09.828 --> 00:00:12.080
I'm telling you the past.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.157
The past will tell you the future.

00:00:14.157 --> 00:00:15.984
It's always the same game.

00:00:18.414 --> 00:00:20.180
I would tell you if I'm 
a photographer right now

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.096
the number one place 
I would build an audience on,

00:00:22.096 --> 00:00:24.380
number one, is Snapchat.

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:28.551
I predict in 2016 that 
Snapchat will have a

00:00:28.551 --> 00:00:30.081
number one, two or three

00:00:30.081 --> 00:00:32.721
spot in the most important 
apps in the world.

00:00:35.572 --> 00:00:37.261
(ding)

00:00:41.044 --> 00:00:43.062
Twitter has a firehose problem.

00:00:43.062 --> 00:00:44.619
Twitter has gotten noisy.

00:00:44.619 --> 00:00:46.672
Twitter is noisy as hell.

00:00:46.672 --> 00:00:47.881
Twitter's struggling.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.018
People don't understand it.

00:00:49.018 --> 00:00:50.454
It's losing attention.

00:00:52.925 --> 00:00:54.883
(ding)

00:00:59.007 --> 00:01:00.928
Nintendo.

00:01:00.928 --> 00:01:01.688
- [Stephanie] Why?

00:01:01.688 --> 00:01:03.594
- Because they're fucking up.

00:01:03.594 --> 00:01:04.683
Like there's no 15 year old,

00:01:04.683 --> 00:01:06.841
the fact that Nintendo 
is not winning

00:01:06.841 --> 00:01:09.052
in app gaming is ludicrous.

00:01:12.286 --> 00:01:14.539
(buzzer)

00:01:16.704 --> 00:01:19.895
I am predicting that Facebook
acquires Instagram.

00:01:21.647 --> 00:01:23.452
(ding)

